issues.body:
Prerequisite for cond-0531 live-route observation. Carry the accepted design canonical AI/billing-provider axis, Route.quota_provider, explicitly; never infer it from harness, profile, model, or provider_route/auth transport.

Owned writer-to-consumer flow:
- conductor launch writers copy the already resolved Route.quota_provider into the ordinary, managed-v1, and managed-v2 terminal creation/reservation request contracts;
- fork request and terminal-service boundaries forward that exact value;
- v1 and isolated-v2 terminal stores persist assigned_quota_provider with additive migrations, and creation commits it with the terminal row;
- restart readback and the shared terminal projection return the persisted value to API/CLI/dashboard consumers without consulting ambient routing state.

Compatibility and honesty:
- legacy rows and older optional request payloads may be absent and remain explicitly absent/unobserved; no backfill or profile/harness inference;
- a missing legacy column is migrated before use; an unreadable or failed schema/read does not become an absent value or a guessed provider;
- provider_route remains auth_transport and is never consumed as quota_provider;
- the projection/display follow-on cond-0531 is blocked on this persisted carrier so it cannot ship a provider-optional or half-built mechanism.

Write boundary excludes Lane A routing algebra/registries/defaults, Lane B successor policy, Lane F registered-wait/registered-wait-monitor records, and Lane G follow-on route work. Lane A confirmed cond-0540 owns launch precedence only and does not persist or observe provider identity.

Done when production writer->request->DB->restart readback->shared projection is proven for ordinary, managed-v1, and managed-v2 terminals; old-row absence and schema-unreadable behavior are distinct; and mutation-reverting each writer/persistence/projection leg makes a focused test fail.

Parent cond-0529 has landed registries, composition, aliases, launch-route metadata, recursion gates, and identity persistence, but production still provisions and launches registered profiles from static profiles/*.md. compose_all and compose_one are tested for equivalence yet have no production provision or launch consumer, leaving static files as a second authoring authority.

Done when:
- every registered legacy and nonlegacy profile alias is provisioned and launched from composer output;
- static profiles/*.md cease being an independent source for registered profiles, while project and external overlays retain their explicitly file-backed behavior;
- all 58 established profile names, exact composed bytes, and all 55 declared Route tuples remain unchanged;
- provision, agent-store lookup, spawn, and doctor consume the same composed source and fail distinctly for absent versus unreadable overlays;
- installed-wheel operation succeeds without a repository checkout;
- one production provision -> agent-store -> spawn/doctor test fails if composer consumption is bypassed;
- inverse mutations for provision, lookup, spawn, doctor, alias, and wheel wiring each turn a named test red and restore green.

Exact first-child scope excludes accepted-spec S6 content migration, S7 task-name predicate removal, and any S2 reporting/goal-role consumer retarget. Those remain separate follow-on children so this change only establishes one canonical production source. Preserve current role/harness registries, Route identity, model/effort behavior, external overlay semantics, and every already-merged identity lane.
